  "preamble": "Deretroflexion of the retroflex lateral [ɭ] to the alveolar lateral [l]. Proto-Dravidian *ḷ, which Wikipedia's Proto-Dravidian consonant table gives as [ɭ], appears as l in the Kurux (Kurukh) reflexes that Wiktionary lists for *āḷ 'person', *kaḷam 'open place' and *uḷḷi 'onion'; the Kurux entry आल gives /aːl/. A note to Wikipedia's Kurukh consonant table describes the change as a merger of *ɭ with /l/, and the table has no retroflex lateral. Not every Kurux reflex of a *ḷ etymon has l: Wiktionary gives मुरमा for *mūḷV- 'bone marrow'. Tamil and Malayalam keep the retroflex lateral (ஆள், ആൾ from *āḷ).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deretroflexion, Merger",
  "languageExamples": [
